                <pb facs="0237" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3709: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-30T20:00:00+08:00">January 30, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 30—6:49 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of January 27, I have now decided that the exigencies
                    justify my requesting that the landing forces from American vessels be increased
                    at the earliest moment possible.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
